S1q22

We have uncovered the full attack chain… Or almost. MITRE ATT&CK also mention the "reconnaissance" phase, when an attacker tries to gather information about their target before trying to compromise them. Here, it would be before they logged into Anne's machine. You cannot always find the full extent of that activity, as it might not touch the company's network (think social media, for which they do not have logs).

What is the last search the threat actor made on the company's website?


 it would be before they logged into Anne's machine

we check with threat actor IPS found previously + we add search 

let A=
PassiveDns
| where domain contains "traintofokke.boo"
| where rdata matches regex @"^(\d{1,3}\.){3}\d{1,3}$"
| distinct rdata;
InboundNetworkEvents
| where src_ip has_any (A)
| where timestamp <= datetime(10/25/2025, 7:56:03 AM)
| where url contains "search" and url contains "fokke.nl"
| order by timestamp desc 



https://fokke.nl/search=no+more+shipping
https://fokke.nl/search=bringing+the+company+to+a+standstill
https://fokke.nl/search=where+to+hit+them+so+it+hurts+most
https://fokke.nl/search=yearly+profit+of+the+company

based on the   it would be before they logged into Anne's machine

we take the url just before login time (10/25/2025, 7:56:03 AM)

response 
